{
  "rationale": "Recent gains are roughly 100 times smaller than the required record increment, while repeated local searches return to the same basin. This supports reducing refinement and incumbent concentration, not spending more on numerical polishing. Favor hybridization and structural changes, reserve meaningful budget for untested formulations, and retain lower-scoring but topologically distinct intermediates. Keep fidelity settings unchanged because there is no timing evidence that they are responsible for the stall.",
